# text = In the year 1850 , shortly after the famine in Ireland and the establishment of the Incumbered Estates Court , which very much altered landed property there , a measure was prepared under the auspices of Sir William Somerville — the present Lord Athlumney — dealing with the subject , but owing to a change of Government it was laid aside .
