# text_id = 1617
# text = It has been said by the greatest soldier who ever flourished — at least in modern times — that the Thanks of the House of Commons were a compliment the most appreciated by military men , and that , next to the favour of their Sovereign , the acknowledgment of their services by Parliament was the reward which they most valued .
