# text_id = 1626
# text = In the case of the Dundalk election in 1826 , and the elections of Dublin and Rye in 1831 , petitions were presented complaining of the conduct of the returning officers , and because they were considered to be in the nature of election petitions , though not directly assuming that form , the House refused to receive them .
