# text = But he asked the House whether a manufacture , which amounted to upwards of £ 60,000,000 per annum in value , was not also a question of great national interest and importance ; and was it not the duty of Parliament to secure , as far as possible , this vast manufacture from accidents in the supply of the raw material ?
