# text = There were various disturbing causes still in Ireland — a strong feeling of nationality , which the Protestant clergy seemed all of a sudden to have taken up — disatisfaction about land and education ; but he had invariably held that religious animosity , produced by religious ascendancy , had hitherto tainted and poisoned ; the whole atmosphere of Ireland .
