# text_id = 1650
# text = In our old law books it was laid down that the sheriff was entitled to summon all the people of the county to attend him on such occasions — to call out the posse comitatus , as it was termed — and by a Statute of Henry V. the neglect to attend such summons was punishable by fine and imprisonment .
