# text_id = 1652
# text = It was declared by the , Courts in Dublin that the pious purposes for which the money was left were superstitious ; that the Catholic inhabitants were ; not entitled to vote , and that in fact the ; Rev. Mr. Gregg was virtually entitled to pocket the amount annually , and to disregard the conditions of the bequest .
