# text_id = 1667
# text = Those who held ultramontane opinions in Ireland seemed to ask how it was that the British Government had not adopted in that country during the Rebellion of 1798 the course which they were now pressing upon the Emperor of Russia , although the position of Ireland towards England in that year was analogous to that of Poland towards Russia at present .
