# text_id = 1669
# text = THE DUKE OF MONTROSE thought that neither the contractors nor creditors , when they entered into their engagements , believed in the possibility of any railway being made bankrupt ; and shareholders would certainly refuse to embark in any undertaking if they knew that , by so doing , they would render themselves liable for a larger amount than their shares .
