# text_id = 1677
# text = Roman Catholics would probably most strongly object to having their children instructed in the tenets of Paley or Bentham by Professors who accepted those tenets as true , but they had no objection to having those works used as text books in Catholic Colleges , where the teachers would , in reading them , point out what they considered their errors .
