# text_id = 1678
# text = He thought he might without exaggeration assert that a great number of Irish landlords paid no attention whatever to their property , either by themselves or their agents , beyond collecting the rents twice a year , and it would be beneficial to the country if such landlords were compelled by law to look after their property a little more .
