# text = MR. ALDERMAN LUSK said , that the charge against the metropolitan Members of neglecting to bring the rights of their constituents before the Committee was groundless , inasmuch as the hon . Member for Southwark ( Mr. Locke ) had stated the case of the metropolitan consumers to the House when the Bill was introduced before the Committee was appointed .
