# text_id = 1703
# text = MR. DARBY GRIFFITH said , with reference to the remarks of the hon . Member for Oldham ( Mr. Hibbert ) , that if any change took place from private executions it would most certainly not be to public executions , but to the total abolition of capital punishment ; the national aversion to secresy would enforce this abolition .
