# text_id = 1711
# text = The First Lord of the Admiralty had stated that he would abandon Deptford , and , after a time , Woolwich , as far as shipbuilding was concerned ; but Deptford was the best store receiving place in the Kingdom ; and it would therefore be a great waste of money to spend £ 70,000 for new storehouses at Woolwich .
