# text_id = 1744
# text = MR. AYRTON said , there was no analogy between the Academy of Music and the Geographical Society , which was essentially a public society , with public objects , whereas the Academy was merely for the purpose of giving persons a superior knowledge of music , and thereby enabling them to earn larger salaries than they otherwise could command .
