# text_id = 1754
# text = MR. STEPHEN CAVE said , in reply , that by the 239th section of the Merchant Shipping Act of 1854 , breach of duty , or neglect of duty , or drunkenness on the part of the master or crew , tending to the loss or damage of a ship , or danger to those on board , was a misdemeanour .
