# text_id = 1771
# text = Sir , I think the general feeling of the House must be that the discussion of an Irish question , and particularly that which relates to the security of life and property , ought to be conducted with great seriousness and earnestness of purpose ; but , if possible , without heat , and with a careful avoidance of exaggeration .
