# text_id = 1778
# text = A capitalization of the Regium Donum for fourteen years was a very inadequate realization of the just expectations of those Presbyterian Protestants whose ancestors in the beginning of the 17th century emigrated from Scotland to Ireland for the furtherance of British purposes , and who by their skill and industry reclaimed the province of Ulster from a state of semi-barbarism .
