# text_id = 1789
# text = The noble Lord at the head of the Government had , on a previous occasion , stated that merit was only the opinion which one man formed of another , that any opinion was sure to be disputed , and that it was a utopian idea to suppose that under any system individuals could be selected on account of merit alone .
