# text_id = 1793
# text = These Chinese Ministers , after the receipt of that letter , remained from the 30th of March until the middle of June , but no one can say that they were justified in expecting either Lord Elgin or Mr. Bruce to negotiate at Shanghai , when they had received an intimation that another and more natural course had been decided upon .
