# text_id = 1815
# text = He had entered the House prepared to listen with great attention to the arguments urged by the old and practised debaters there , and though nothing would induce him to betray the trust which his constituents had reposed in him , still if he were convinced that opinions he formerly held were wrong , he would have resigned his seat rather than record a vote which his conscience did not ratify .
