# text_id = 1817
# text = Many un- successful undertakings might be started on the principle of limited liability , and he confessed that when the principle was first introduced he looked upon it with jealousy , but experience had shown that the principle of limited liability had extended itself , and was practically successful in the mercantile world , as applied to companies , and why should it not be extended to other contracts ?
