# text_id = 1819
# text = MR. W. ORMSBY GORE said , that in 1846 the late Sir Robert Peel , with that spirit of liberality and generosity which characterized his conduct with reference to Ireland , and which had in a great measure been inherited by the right hon . Baronet who bore his name , had introduced a Bill on this subject , which was followed by another in 1848 , and another in 1857 .
