# text_id = 1824
# text = The period of the articles of clerkship was five years , and a person could not be admitted as an attorney unless he had served those five years ; but it was proposed in the Bill of the Society to admit gentlemen who had taken degrees at the Universities after a service of three , under articles of five years , — of course subject to the usual examination .
