# text_id = 1827
# text = Wishing to maintain the Sunday as a day of rest , and yet feeling that the Bill , if carried with all its exceptions , was liable to objection , he thought the best course to adopt would be that which was recommended by the noble Lord the Chairman of Committees — because by taking that course they would , at all events , check the system of Sunday trading .
