# text_id = 1836
# text = If , for example , an owner borrowed money under the Lands Improvement Acts , and laid it out upon the land , even though it turned out the very next day that he was not the rightful owner and had no right to effect the loan , yet whoever the owner might be , the charge would attach itself to the land until the debt was entirely paid off .
