# text_id = 1847
# text = Negotiations had been entered upon , in the course of which the Earl of Elgin and Baron Gros were invited to go to Pekin , and when they said they required an escort each of 1,000 men the Chinese then no longer wished them to come , because they knew that our Ambassadors would then be safe against the treachery of which it was intended they were to be the victims .
