# text_id = 1852
# text = But on one subject he thought they were all agreed — that whatever might be the decision of the House , it should be founded on clear data ; that there should be no misunderstanding as to the proposals of the Government ; and that when once there was a decision of the House , embodied in an Act of Parliament , it should be strictly observed by the executive Government .
