# text_id = 1854
# text = The illustrious Duke had said these questions were all matters of money ; he ( Earl Grey ) was prepared , however , at the proper time , to show that the adoption of his recommendations would cause no increase of expense , but , on the contrary , would tend to economy by reducing pensions and various charges to a larger amount than the new expenses it might create .
