# text_id = 1855
# text = He was at a loss to understand how a Gentleman of the political experience of the Chancellor of the Exchequer could have committed such a mistake in tactics as to lead the great bulk of the Liberal party to show apparently their disinclination to deal with this subject by taking them into the lobby the previous night to vote against the Instruction of the hon . Member for Northamptonshire .
