# text_id = 1858
# text = MR. ALDERMAN LUSK considered it was strange that the army of a country whose manufactures were never equalled , whose ships could sail against any ships in the world , and who could successfully compete at farming with any nation on the earth , should cost more , man for man , than the army of any other country , and that they should be always in trouble respecting it .
