# text_id = 1861
# text = The Resolution was moved and seconded by two of the most eminent Members of the Manchester and Peace party in this House , the Members for Birmingham and Ashton ; and our economical Chancellor of the Exchequer was the most eloquent exponent of the national dissatisfaction with the Minister who had not shown a bolder front to Trance , when our economy had left him no front to show .
