# text_id = 1863
# text = He did not impute blame to the Attorney General , who had acted , he believed , bonâ fide , though , as he thought , in an unconstitutional manner , in erroneously refusing to grant a writ of error when it was applied for on behalf of Mr. Pigott ; hut as the matter was an important one , he felt it his duty to bring it before Parliament .
