# text_id = 1864
# text = CAPTAIN ARCHDALL said , that after the statement of the noble Marquess , that further inquiry was to take place , no good purpose could be gained by prolonging the present debate ; but , as an old Inniskilling officer , he felt for the character of the regiment , and he therefore regarded with satisfaction the testimony borne to its former good condition by the Commander - in - Chief .
