# text_id = 1874
# text = MR. COWPER said , he did not think this an occasion on which he could permit himself to follow the right hon . Gentleman through the personalities on which he had spent so much time , and he altogether declined to enter into any discussion on the private character of the Duke of Buccleuch , which was not , he was happy to say , the question before the House .
