# text_id = 1876
# text = The truth is , that , with the exception of the Artillery corps , respecting which peculiar care was taken from the very earliest time , the European army was very ill organized , and in so inferior a state of discipline that the officers of the Company placed almost their entire reliance upon the Sepoy troops , under European command , and upon the regiments of the Line .
