# text_id = 1879
# text = Two high authorities — Lord Overstone and the first Lord Ashburton — gave evidence on the subject before a Parliamentary Committee in 1844 , the first objecting to any change of the law , and the second expressing himself as , upon the whole , favourable to limited liability , on the ground that it would bring out a great deal of capital now lying dormant or sent to other countries .
