# text_id = 1885
# text = Even when the Commission — the appointment of which was censured by the right hon . Gentleman ( Mr. Lowe ) as wholly unnecessary — made its valuable Report , if the Government had felt disposed to give effect to its recommendations , it would have been impossible to do so without exciting such an amount of opposition throughout the country as must have neutralized altogether the efforts of the Government .
