# text_id = 1887
# text = MR. CHICHESTER FORTESCUE said , that at that time of night , he would not give any detailed reasons for the opinion which he entertained that his noble Friend had failed altogether to vindicate his own consistency in introducing a Bill this Session , the principle of which directly contradicted his Motion of last year , and the Resolution which he had proposed in the Select Committee only two years ago .
