# text_id = 1890
# text = For his own part , he held that the maintenance of a Church based on the principle of freedom of conscience and the right of private judgment was in itself a great advantage to any community which was subject to the rigid enforcement of ecclesiastical discipline , and in Ireland , were it not for the Established Church , there would be a state of things such as existed in Spain .
