# text_id = 1898
# text = If every portion of the income derived from the money now proposed to be taken were applied to the reduction of the fees of court it would not reduce them more than from 8 to 4 per cent ; that is to say , out of every £ 100 paid by the suitor he would have to pay , as fees of court , £ 4 instead of £ 8 .
