# text_id = 1900
# text = The object of that Convention was to carry out an arrangement which had been acceded to by the late Government , and under which the Postmaster General of this country was to provide for the conveyance of mails on stated days from certain ports in England to certain ports in the United States , and the United States were to provide for the conveyance of mails the reverse way .
