# text_id = 1921
# text = He thought that there was great force in what the hon . Gentleman said with regard to the duties on tea and sugar , and he trusted that whoever might in future occupy the office of Chancellor of the Exchequer would be enabled to adopt a system which would give the commercial community a larger outlook with respect to these duties than they could have under a provisional arrangement .
