# text_id = 1924
# text = The Spanish Government , while they take some steps which might be commended , while they arm some cruisers to check the slave trade , do allow their officials , and more especially the planters in the Isle of Cuba , to derive enormous profits — as much as 70 , 80 , and 100 per cent — from this horrible traffic , which is to us a subject of abhorrence .
