# text_id = 1928
# text = With respect to the intention of the Government , he had to say that communications had passed between the French and English Governments upon this subject , and though at present nothing had been settled , the subject was still under consideration , and he believed it would be better to wait until the Report had appeared before the question was considered , whether any amendment in the Convention was desirable ?
