# text_id = 1931
# text = THE LORD CHANCELLOR said , that so far as he was concerned , he should be most willing to postpone the Committee on the Divorce Bill till a later hour of the evening in order that the noble Marquess might have precedence ; but he must for the credit of the House protest against its being supposed that they could not entertain more than one subject on any evening .
