# text = LORD STANLEY OF ALDERLEY said , he was informed by the Home Secretary that the Bill was entirely unnecessary , as the case was provided form the Highways Act , by which such contracts were prohibited under a penalty and the Highways Act of last Session provided that all qualifications and disqualifications of surveyors of highways , and waywardens which existed under the old law should continue in force .
