# text_id = 1935
# text = The property tax was a reasonable and legitimate tax to meet the requirements of the country — it was the ancient and proper means of raising revenue ; and although vestries had power to impose a tax analogous to the income tax , common sense told them that the proper way was to raise the tax from property , and this was done throughout the length and breadth of the country .
