# text_id = 1936
# text = When he saw the vast undeveloped resources of India , and the poverty of the people , it appeared to him that the only way to extricate the country from its difficulties was to increase the tax paying power of the people by means of increased and cheap facilities of conveyance , and by great public works , which could not be executed except by public loans for the special purpose .
