# text_id = 1944
# text = The boon granted by the Bill would be a boon entirely to the Metropolitan Board of Works , and not one to the metropolis at all ; and unless the House were satisfied that the money would be wisely expended , and that those persons would obtain the contracts who sent in the lowest tenders , he did not think that additional powers ought to be given to that Board .
