# text_id = 1946
# text = I will only glance at the dangerous , I may almost say immoral doctrine , that whilst the German States may have entered singly , and as independent States , into a treaty , or may have accepted it , as in the case of the Treaty of 1852 , they are at liberty to repudiate its engagements when acting in the aggregate , and forming the Germanic Confederation .
