# text_id = 1955
# text = THE MARQUESS OF WESTMEATH said , that 4,190 persons had been killed or injured in the streets of London between 1858 and 1865 ; and therefore he was justified in concluding that there was not proper control of the traffic ; and he attributed the accidents to the furious driving of light carts , which were often in charge of youths who thought it good fun to drive recklessly .
