# text = Supposing a change of Government should take place , and supposing the new Ministry should allege that some Greek had gone to a Junior Lord of the Admiralty , and made a corrupt proposal , and , acting upon that allegation , should entreat the parties to the Treaty of Vienna to refuse their assent to the cession , what would the House think of the morality of such a proceeding ?
