# text_id = 1963
# text = Being an admirer , in the main , of the present foreign policy of the noble Earl at the Foreign Office — having more especially sympathized with his Italian policy , and having , in his humble way , taken the greatest interest in Italian unity — he regretted he could not say that , in his opinion , the action of the Foreign Secretary had been satisfactory in this case .
