# text_id = 1968
# text = The hon . and learned Gentleman seemed to consider the Bill which he asked leave to introduce a small Reform Bill ; but , according to the manner in which the word " Reform " was generally understood in that House , a Bill which merely related to the conduct of elections — to the manner in which votes were to be taken — was not a measure of Parliamentary Reform .
