# text_id = 1969
# text = The truth was that social habits had a greater effect on the consumption of wine , one way or the other , than any amount of duty whatever ; and , judging of the future from the past , he thought the Chancellor of the Exchequer had been exceedingly sanguine in the estimate he had taken of the probable increase of consumption from the proposed reduction in the duties .
