# text_id = 1971
# text = The present time , when , as their Lordships knew , the utmost efforts were being made to promote the spread of monastic institutions in this country , which were expressly struck at by the Act of 1829 , was not a moment to weaken any of the securities which the Bill of 1829 afforded , and for these reasons he should vote against the second reading of the Bill .
