# text_id = 1976
# text = Another point to which be wished to direct the attention of the House was the fact that the amount insured in this country had not increased in the same proportion as the national property , for while in 1835 £ 500,000,000 of value had been insured , in 1855 , notwithstanding that the country had in the meantime made enormous progress in wealth , the amount insured was only £ 800,000,000 .
