# text_id = 1985
# text = It had been said , he knew not on what authority , that a late noble Lord , so long the Leader of that House ( Lord Palmerston ) , had refused to make out his right to vote for the Irish Representative Peerage , because he was afraid that , at some time or other , he might be elected and sent to the House of Lords against his will .
