# text_id = 1995
# text = As a matter of humanity it was right to make a distinction between the manner of treating the sick and the aged poor , and the manner of treating the able - bodied poor ; but , as regarded the principles on which relief should be given under the Poor Law , he maintained those principles ought to be applied to all classes of the poor , without distinction .
