# text_id = 1996
# text = The main point in the whole of these Reports and Acts of Parliament to which he had referred was , that any man entering the Indian army and agreeing to serve a certain number of years , did so upon condition that he should not be superseded by others in his profession , and that at the end of a certain number of years he should retire on a fixed pension .
