# text = He ( Mr. Newdegate ) held in his hand an account of the distress produced in the silk trade by the change made by Mr. Huskisson ; from the evidence of Mr. Grout before the Committee of 1832 , it appeared that before that change in 1826 the people engaged in the trade were prosperous and happy , but afterwards , in 1832 , their condition had miserably deteriorated .
