# text_id = 2001
# text = MR. BLACK maintained that the Bill , if it passed into a law , would , instead of promoting conciliation , lead to the contrary result ; inasmuch as the very fact that the operatives knew that there were tribunals to which disputes between themselves and their masters might be referred for settlement might lead them to start objections which , under other circumstances , they never would have contemplated raising .
