# text_id = 2005
# text = Perhaps the caprice of legislation never went further than in this case , for by the present system clay or stone was liable to be rated when dug from an open quarry , but when brought up from the bowels of the earth by means of shafts and windlasses it was not rated , because it was then regarded as a mine , and it was not a coal mine .
