# text_id = 2006
# text = Then , in 1852 , a Bill was passed through that House — and how such an iniquitous Bill should be passed he could not understand — which gave an additional power to the Westminster Commissioners to issue any amount of bonds they chose , resting on no security whatsoever , and he believed he was right in saying that they made the most prodigious use of that power .
