# text_id = 2010
# text = Where there was a concurrent jurisdiction in a Court of Law and a Court of Equity , it was the right of the subject to choose the one or the other ; and when he asked for relief in a certain court , that court ought not to have power to abdicate its functions because it might be thought more convenient that the question should be decided in another court .
