# text_id = 2021
# text = It was a curious circumstance that the word " permanent " was to be found in several old Irish Ecclesiastical Acts as applied to curates , and that in 14 & 15 Vict. c. 73 , s. 2 , it was declared that in ascertaining the net income of the clergy for the purposes of the Act , the " salaries of permanent and necessary curates " were to be deducted .
