# text_id = 2029
# text = As a rule , everything in the way of permanent improvement — in fitting the farm for the occupancy of the tenant , and for his proper working of his holding — is effected in England by the landlord ; whereas in Ireland the rule — to which , however , there are many noble exceptions — is that the landlord does nothing , the tenant everything that is done .
