# text_id = 2033
# text = He thought that a great indiscretion was committed when , in the triumphal cortège which escorted the Prince of Wales and his bride on their entrance to Dublin , the place of honour was accorded to the 12th Lancers , whose presence called from the people execrations , both loud and deep , and cries of " Duugarvan butchers " — the name by which they are now called in Ireland .
